// Q-1011 A program with no routes that keeps running opens an HTTP port anyway, and does not start when that port is taken
// mode: script
// script: steps.sh
// open-when: Address already in use
// fixed-when: /port taken: [^\n]*runs without a port[^\n]*tick/
// From FEEDBACK72.md §Q-1011 (found on 238dac2, 0.8.6; open on 77ffcd0, 0.8.9). With the
// port taken it stops at once; with it free it says it listens, and answers 404.

// No routes, no server fn: a timer that keeps the program running.
every(500, () => { print("tick") })
